---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const promptParts = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "Task",
    text:
      "State clearly what you want AI to do. A vague task usually produces a vague result.",
    example: "Draft a supplier follow-up email.",
  },
  {
    number: "02",
    title: "Role",
    text:
      "Give AI a useful perspective when specialist framing would improve the result.",
    example: "Act as an operations manager.",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "Context",
    text:
      "Provide the background information AI needs to understand the situation correctly.",
    example: "The shipment is three days late and the customer is waiting.",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Audience",
    text:
      "Tell AI who will read or use the output so it can adjust language, detail and tone.",
    example: "Write for a senior manager.",
  },
  {
    number: "05",
    title: "Output format",
    text:
      "Specify how the answer should be structured instead of leaving the format to chance.",
    example: "Use a short email with subject line and three paragraphs.",
  },
  {
    number: "06",
    title: "Tone",
    text:
      "Define how the response should sound when communication style matters.",
    example: "Professional, polite and firm.",
  },
  {
    number: "07",
    title: "Detail level",
    text:
      "Tell AI whether you need a quick answer, a practical explanation or a detailed analysis.",
    example: "Keep it under 150 words.",
  },
  {
    number: "08",
    title: "Constraints",
    text:
      "Set boundaries, requirements or things the model should avoid.",
    example: "Do not promise a delivery date that has not been confirmed.",
  },
];

const weakVsStrong = [
  {
    label: "WEAK",
    text: "Write an email about a late delivery.",
  },
  {
    label: "STRONGER",
    text:
      "Act as an operations supervisor. Draft a professional email to a supplier about a shipment that is three days late. Ask for the confirmed dispatch status and revised ETA. Keep the email under 150 words, remain polite but firm, and do not make assumptions about the cause of the delay.",
  },
];

const checklist = [
  "Is the task specific?",
  "Have I provided the necessary context?",
  "Does AI know who the output is for?",
  "Have I specified the format I need?",
  "Are important constraints included?",
  "Can the result be reviewed before use?",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Anatomy of a Good Prompt | KRIYANO"
  description="Learn the core parts of a good AI prompt, including task, context, audience, format, tone and constraints, with practical workplace examples."
>
  <article class="article-page">
    <header class="article-hero">
      <div class="container article-hero-grid">
        <div class="article-heading">
          <a href="/learn/" class="back-link">← LEARN</a>

          <div class="article-meta">
            <span>PROMPTING FUNDAMENTALS</span>
            <span>05</span>
            <span>BEGINNER</span>
          </div>

          <h1>
            Anatomy of a
            <span>Good Prompt.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="article-intro">
            Better prompts are not about using complicated wording. They are
            about giving AI enough direction to understand the task, the
            situation and the result you actually need.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="lesson-panel">
          <div class="panel-header">
            <span>LESSON 05</span>
            <span>PROMPTING FUNDAMENTALS</span>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-content">
            <span class="panel-kicker">THE SIMPLE FORMULA</span>

            <strong>
              Clear task + useful context + clear output requirements.
            </strong>

            <p>
              You do not need every prompt element every time. Use the parts
              that reduce ambiguity and improve control.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-footer">
            <span>TASK → CONTEXT → OUTPUT</span>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="article-body-section">
      <div class="container article-layout">
        <aside class="article-sidebar">
          <div class="sidebar-box">
            <span class="sidebar-title">IN THIS GUIDE</span>

            <a href="#good-prompt">What makes a prompt good?</a>
            <a href="#parts">Eight useful prompt parts</a>
            <a href="#comparison">Weak vs stronger prompt</a>
            <a href="#work-example">A real-work example</a>
            <a href="#checklist">Prompt checklist</a>
            <a href="#takeaway">The practical takeaway</a>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <main class="article-content">
          <section id="good-prompt">
            <div class="section-marker">01 / THE CORE IDEA</div>

            <h2>A good prompt reduces uncertainty.</h2>

            <p>
              When AI receives a short instruction with little context, it has
              to make more assumptions about what you want. Some assumptions may
              be reasonable. Others may produce the wrong tone, structure,
              level of detail or even the wrong interpretation of the task.
            </p>

            <p>
              A stronger prompt gives the model enough direction to produce an
              answer that is closer to your actual need on the first attempt.
            </p>

            <div class="concept-box">
              <span>GOOD PROMPTING IS NOT</span>

              <p>
                Writing long or complicated instructions for every task. The
                goal is to include the information that meaningfully changes the
                quality of the result.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="parts">
            <div class="section-marker">02 / PROMPT COMPONENTS</div>

            <h2>Eight building blocks you can use when they matter.</h2>

            <p>
              Not every prompt needs all eight. Think of them as controls you
              can add when you need more precision.
            </p>

            <div class="parts-grid">
              {
                promptParts.map((item) => (
                  <article class="part-card">
                    <span class="part-number">{item.number}</span>

                    <h3>{item.title}</h3>

                    <p>{item.text}</p>

                    <div class="part-example">
                      <span>EXAMPLE</span>
                      <p>{item.example}</p>
                    </div>
                  </article>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="comparison">
            <div class="section-marker">03 / WEAK VS STRONGER</div>

            <h2>Small changes can significantly improve the output.</h2>

            <div class="prompt-comparison">
              {
                weakVsStrong.map((item) => (
                  <div class={`prompt-card ${item.label.toLowerCase()}`}>
                    <span>{item.label}</span>
                    <p>{item.text}</p>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            <p>
              The stronger version tells AI what role is useful, what happened,
              what the email must achieve, how it should sound and what it
              should avoid.
            </p>

            <div class="breakdown">
              <div>
                <span>ROLE</span>
                <p>Operations supervisor</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>TASK</span>
                <p>Draft supplier follow-up email</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>CONTEXT</span>
                <p>Shipment is three days late</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>GOAL</span>
                <p>Get status and revised ETA</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>TONE</span>
                <p>Professional, polite and firm</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>CONSTRAINT</span>
                <p>No unsupported assumptions</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="work-example">
            <div class="section-marker">04 / REAL-WORK EXAMPLE</div>

            <h2>Build the prompt from the situation you actually have.</h2>

            <p>
              Imagine you need AI to help prepare an inventory discrepancy
              summary for management after an investigation.
            </p>

            <div class="work-flow">
              <div class="flow-row">
                <span>01</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Task</strong>
                  <p>
                    Prepare a concise inventory discrepancy summary.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flow-row">
                <span>02</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Context</strong>
                  <p>
                    System stock is 500 units and verified physical stock is
                    476 units. Receiving, outbound and adjustment transactions
                    have already been reviewed.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flow-row">
                <span>03</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Audience</strong>
                  <p>
                    The summary will be sent to the inventory manager.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flow-row">
                <span>04</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Output</strong>
                  <p>
                    Use headings for variance, checks completed, findings and
                    recommended next action.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flow-row">
                <span>05</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Constraint</strong>
                  <p>
                    Do not invent a root cause. State clearly when the cause has
                    not yet been confirmed.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="assembled-prompt">
              <span>ASSEMBLED PROMPT</span>

              <p>
                Act as an inventory control supervisor. Prepare a concise
                inventory discrepancy summary for the inventory manager. System
                stock is 500 units and verified physical stock is 476 units.
                Receiving, outbound and adjustment transactions have already
                been reviewed. Structure the summary with headings for variance,
                checks completed, findings and recommended next action. Do not
                invent a root cause, and clearly state if the cause remains
                unconfirmed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="checklist">
            <div class="section-marker">05 / QUICK CHECK</div>

            <h2>Before sending your prompt, check these six things.</h2>

            <div class="checklist">
              {
                checklist.map((item, index) => (
                  <div class="check-row">
                    <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                    <p>{item}</p>
                    <strong>✓</strong>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            <div class="decision-box">
              <span>DON'T OVERBUILD</span>

              <p>
                If a simple prompt already gives you the result you need, stop
                there. Add more structure only when it improves accuracy,
                consistency or usefulness.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="takeaway">
            <div class="section-marker">06 / PRACTICAL TAKEAWAY</div>

            <h2>Prompting is mostly about clarity.</h2>

            <p>
              Start with the task. Add the context that changes the answer. Then
              specify the output requirements that matter.
            </p>

            <div class="takeaway-flow">
              <div>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>Define</strong>
                <p>What should AI do?</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>Contextualise</strong>
                <p>What does AI need to know?</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>Specify</strong>
                <p>What should the output look like?</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>04</span>
                <strong>Review</strong>
                <p>Did the result meet the need?</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tool-callout">
              <div>
                <span class="tool-kicker">BUILD IT WITH KRIYANO</span>

                <h3>Use the Prompt Builder to structure your next prompt.</h3>

                <p>
                  Add your task, role, audience, context, output format, tone,
                  detail level and constraints in one guided workspace.
                </p>
              </div>

              <a href="/tools/prompt-builder/" class="button button-primary">
                Open Prompt Builder
              </a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="next-lesson">
            <div>
              <span class="next-label">NEXT LESSON</span>

              <h2>How to Give AI Better Context</h2>

              <p>
                Learn which background details improve AI output and how to
                provide useful context without making prompts unnecessarily long.
              </p>
            </div>

            <a
  href="/learn/prompting-fundamentals/how-to-give-ai-better-context/"
  class="next-status"
>
  CONTINUE →
</a>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
